From 23eaf3b5c1a755e3193480c76fb29414be648688 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leon Romanovsky <leonro@mellanox.com>
Date: Wed, 31 Jul 2019 11:38:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] RDMA/mlx5: Release locks during notifier unregister

The below kernel panic was observed when created bond mode LACP
with GRE tunnel on top. The reason to it was not released spinlock
during mlx5 notify unregsiter sequence.

[  234.562007] BUG: scheduling while atomic: sh/10900/0x00000002
[  234.563005] Preemption disabled at:
[  234.566864] 
diff --git a/drivers/infiniband/hw/mlx5/main.c b/drivers/infiniband/hw/mlx5/main.c
index c2a5780cb394..e12a4404096b 100644
--- a/drivers/infiniband/hw/mlx5/main.c
+++ b/drivers/infiniband/hw/mlx5/main.c
@@ -5802,13 +5802,12 @@ static void mlx5_ib_unbind_slave_port(struct mlx5_ib_dev *ibdev,
 		return;
 	}

-	if (mpi->mdev_events.notifier_call)
-		mlx5_notifier_unregister(mpi->mdev, &mpi->mdev_events);
-	mpi->mdev_events.notifier_call = NULL;
-
 	mpi->ibdev = NULL;

 	spin_unlock(&port->mp.mpi_lock);
+	if (mpi->mdev_events.notifier_call)
+		mlx5_notifier_unregister(mpi->mdev, &mpi->mdev_events);
+	mpi->mdev_events.notifier_call = NULL;
 	mlx5_remove_netdev_notifier(ibdev, port_num);
 	spin_lock(&port->mp.mpi_lock);

-- 
2.25.1

Code statements:
```c
if (mpi->mdev_events.notifier_call)
		mlx5_notifier_unregister(mpi->mdev, &mpi->mdev_events);
mpi->mdev_events.notifier_call = NULL;
spin_unlock(&port->mp.mpi_lock);
```

Code statements:
```c
if (mpi->mdev_events.notifier_call)
		mlx5_notifier_unregister(mpi->mdev, &mpi->mdev_events);
mpi->mdev_events.notifier_call = NULL;
spin_unlock(&port->mp.mpi_lock);
```

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
spin_lock(&port->mp.mpi_lock);
if (mpi->mdev_events.notifier_call)
    mlx5_notifier_unregister(mpi->mdev, &mpi->mdev_events);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the spinlock `mpi_lock` is held while calling `mlx5_notifier_unregister`, which can lead to a situation where the thread attempts to sleep while still holding the lock. This violates the atomic context rules of the kernel, resulting in a kernel panic due to scheduling while atomic.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
spin_unlock(&port->mp.mpi_lock);
if (mpi->mdev_events.notifier_call)
    mlx5_notifier_unregister(mpi->mdev, &mpi->mdev_events);
spin_lock(&port->mp.mpi_lock);
```
Reason:
The fix involves releasing the spinlock before calling `mlx5_notifier_unregister`, allowing the thread to safely sleep if necessary. After unregistering, the spinlock is reacquired, ensuring that the critical section is protected while maintaining proper atomic context.

